# ============================================================================
# Wide table compliance case e26
#
# A test case for core-spec/wide_table_semantics.md, the Wide Table Query
# Interface (Layer 3), as an ost script (apache/ossie#501). The argument to
# executeLower is the query under test, in the JSON binding of Section 3.7.
# executeLower lowers it to a Layer 2 query (Section 5), and the lowering
# raises an error of Section 8. The case requires only the code at the
# start of the error. README.md gives the rules for cases.
#
# Run, from the root of the repository:
#   uv run --project ost ost -d compliance compliance/wide_table/e26_no_step_from_one_side.ost
# ============================================================================

# The "retail" fixture has the tables and values of retail/retail.sql.
connect("retail");
set("doubleDigits", 2);

# The model is retail/retail_model.ossie.yaml.
modelFile("retail_model", "retail/retail_model.ossie.yaml");

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# e26. No step from the one side of a OneToMany relationship.
# Question: How many customers are there per visit?
# customers_to_visits is declared from customers, as OneToMany, so a step
# crosses it from visits to customers only, and customers does not reach
# visits. The error names visits.visit_id and customers.customer_count.
# Spec: 4, 8
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
executeLower("retail_model", {
  "dimensions": ["visits.visit_id"],
  "metrics": ["customers.customer_count"]
});
> error: E_NO_PATH: metric customers.customer_count does not reach visits, the dataset of dimension visits.visit_id, and nor does any other metric

# End e26_no_step_from_one_side.ost
